# Architecture and Design Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_architecture
description: Standards for maintaining proper architecture and design patterns
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:js|jsx|ts|tsx)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)component|architecture|structure|design"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing architecture and design:

      ## Monorepo Structure
      - Organize packages by domain or functionality (e.g., apps/, packages/)
      - Use pnpm workspaces for dependency management
      - Implement centralized build configuration with inheritance
      - Configure cross-package testing with shared configuration
      - Establish clear package boundaries and interfaces

      ## Component Architecture
      - Follow atomic design principles (atoms, molecules, organisms, templates, pages)
      - Implement unidirectional data flow (props down, events up)
      - Separate UI, business logic, and data access concerns
      - Use composition over inheritance for component reuse
      - Implement container/presentation pattern for complex components

      ## Internationalization
      - Configure i18n framework with namespaced translation files
      - Implement locale detection and switching
      - Extract all UI strings into translation resources
      - Handle RTL/LTR layout differences with directional styles
      - Format dates, numbers, and currencies according to locale standards

      ## Security
      - Use role-based authorization
      - Validate all user inputs with strong typing and schemas
      - Apply Content Security Policy and other security headers

      ## Performance
      - Implement dynamic imports for route-based code splitting
      - Optimize bundle size with tree shaking and code elimination
      - Use concurrency for non-interdependent promises.

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new component structure"
    output: "Component follows atomic design principles with clear separation of concerns and efficient data flow patterns"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>
